{
  "title": "What's this? Whose is that?",
  "title_target": "Энэ юу вэ? Тэр хэний юм бэ?",
  "goal": "Point at things, name them, and say whose they are — while seeing for the first time how Mongolian closes a sentence with *юм* and *вэ*.",
  "bekal": [
    "point at and name the things around you with *энэ* and *тэр*",
    "ask *юу вэ* and *хэний юм бэ*, and answer both",
    "use the plural only when you need it — and know when you don't"
  ],
  "dialogs": [
    {
      "title": "Яриа — Ангид",
      "intro": "Budi's first day of class. Sarnai is tidying the desk, and Budi asks about things he doesn't know the names of yet.",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Буди:",
          "text": "[Багш|Baksh] [аа|aa], [энэ|EH-neh] [юу|yuu] [вэ|veh]?",
          "id": "Teacher, what's this?",
          "literal": "teacher O, this what Q?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Сарнай:",
          "text": "[Энэ|EH-neh] [ном|nom]. [Монгол|MON-gol] [хэлний|KHEL-nii] [ном|nom].",
          "id": "It's a book. A Mongolian book.",
          "literal": "this book. Mongolian language's book."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Буди:",
          "text": "[Тэр|Ter] [ч|ch] [бас|bas] [ном|nom] [уу|uu]?",
          "id": "Is that a book too?",
          "literal": "that too also book Q?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Сарнай:",
          "text": "[Үгүй|Ü-güi], [тэр|ter] [дэвтэр|DEV-ter]. [Ном|Nom] [биш|bish].",
          "id": "No, that's a notebook. Not a book for reading.",
          "literal": "no, that notebook. book not."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Буди:",
          "text": "[Тэр|Ter] [дэвтэр|DEV-ter] [хэний|KHEH-nii] [юм|yum] [бэ|beh]?",
          "id": "Whose notebook is that?",
          "literal": "that notebook whose thing Q?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Сарнай:",
          "text": "[Тэр|Ter] [Болдын|BOL-diin] [дэвтэр|DEV-ter].",
          "id": "It's Bold's notebook.",
          "literal": "that Bold's notebook."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Буди:",
          "text": "[Болд|Bold] [хэн|khen] [бэ|beh]?",
          "id": "Who's Bold?",
          "literal": "Bold who Q?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Сарнай:",
          "text": "[Болд|Bold] [бол|bol] [миний|MI-nii] [оюутан|o-YUU-tan]. [Тэр|Ter] [маргааш|mar-GAASH] [ирнэ|IR-neh].",
          "id": "Bold is my student. He's coming tomorrow.",
          "literal": "Bold as-for my student. he tomorrow comes."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Буди:",
          "text": "[Энэ|EH-neh] [хэдэн|KHEH-den] [ном|nom] [бэ|beh]?",
          "id": "How many books are these?",
          "literal": "this how-many book Q?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Сарнай:",
          "text": "[Гурван|GUR-van] [ном|nom]. [Бүгд|Bügd] [шинэ|SHI-neh].",
          "id": "Three books. They're all new.",
          "literal": "three book. all new."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Буди:",
          "text": "[Энэ|EH-neh] [ном|nom] [хэдэн|KHEH-den] [төгрөг|TÖG-rög] [вэ|veh]?",
          "id": "How many tugriks is this book?",
          "literal": "this book how-many tugrik Q?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Сарнай:",
          "text": "[Мэдэхгүй|MEH-dekh-güi]. [Тэр|Ter] [миний|MI-nii] [ном|nom] [биш|bish], [сургуулийн|sur-GUU-liin] [ном|nom].",
          "id": "I don't know. It's not my book, it's the school's.",
          "literal": "know-not. that my book not, school's book."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Буди:",
          "text": "[Ойлголоо|OIL-go-lō]. [Тэгвэл|TEG-vel] [энэ|EH-neh] [бал|bal] [хэний|KHEH-nii] [бэ|beh]?",
          "id": "I see. Then whose pen is this?",
          "literal": "understood. then this pen whose Q?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Сарнай:",
          "text": "[Тэр|Ter] [чинийх|CHI-niikh] [шүү|shüü]! [Чи|Chi] [сая|sa-YA] [ширээн|shi-RĒN] [дээр|dēr] [тавьсан|TAV'-san].",
          "id": "It's yours! You just put it on the desk.",
          "literal": "that yours you-know! you just-now desk top put."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Буди:",
          "text": "[Өө|Öö], [үнэн|Ü-nen] [юм|yum] [байна|BAI-n]! [Уучлаарай|UUCH-laa-rai].",
          "id": "Oh, that's right! Sorry.",
          "literal": "oh, true thing is! sorry."
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        "**Энэ = this, тэр = that.** Both can work as determiners (*энэ ном* — this book) or as pronouns (*Энэ юу вэ?* — What's this?). ⚠️ Remember that *тэр* also means \"he/she\" — *Тэр багш* can mean \"that teacher\" or \"he/she is a teacher\", and only intonation tells them apart.",
        "**Юм means \"thing\", but at the end of a sentence it softens.** *Хэний юм бэ?* is literally \"whose thing?\", and *Үнэн юм байна* is literally \"true thing is\" — naturally, \"oh, that's right\". Think of *юм* as English \"actually\" or \"turns out\".",
        "⚠️ **The possessive suffix -ын / -ийн attaches to the owner, not the thing owned.** *Болд**ын** дэвтэр* — \"Bold**'s** notebook\". The order is exactly like English *'s*: owner first, then the thing — so this one comes easily.",
        "**Бол marks the topic of the sentence**, like \"as for\". *Болд **бол** миний оюутан* — \"Bold is my student\". It's optional, but it makes a sentence sound tidy when you introduce something for the first time.",
        "**Биш negates nouns.** *Ном биш* = \"not a book\". ⚠️ Don't use *үгүй* here — *үгүй* is a stand-alone answer (\"no\"), not a negator inside a sentence."
      ],
      "grammars": [
        {
          "title": "The possessive suffix: -ын, -ийн, -ы, -и, -н",
          "body": [
            "Five forms, one meaning: \"of, belonging to\". What decides the form is **the last letter of the owner word** and **its vowel group** — two things you already know from the vowel harmony page at the front."
          ],
          "table": {
            "head": [
              "Word ends in",
              "Suffix",
              "Example",
              "Meaning"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "consonant, back group",
                "**-ын**",
                "*Болд* → *Болд**ын***",
                "Bold's"
              ],
              [
                "consonant, front group",
                "**-ийн**",
                "*гэр* → *гэр**ийн***",
                "the house's"
              ],
              [
                "*-н*",
                "**-ы / -ий**",
                "*оюутан* → *оюутн**ы***",
                "the student's"
              ],
              [
                "long vowel or diphthong",
                "**-гийн / -гын**",
                "*эмээ* → *эмээ**гийн***",
                "grandmother's"
              ],
              [
                "*-ь* or *-и*",
                "**-йн**",
                "*морь* → *мор**ийн***",
                "the horse's"
              ]
            ]
          },
          "after": [
            "Don't memorize this table now. All you need to take away is one sentence: **the suffix always sounds like \"-iin\" or \"-in\", and it sticks to the owner.** The exact form will come by itself with use.",
            "⚠️ For pronouns, the forms are irregular and must be memorized because they're so frequent: *би* → ***миний***, *чи* → ***чиний***, *та* → ***таны***, *тэр* → ***түүний***, *бид* → ***бидний***, *тэд* → ***тэдний***."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Plurals — and why you rarely need them",
          "body": [
            "Mongolian has plural suffixes, but uses them far less than English. If the number is clear from a numeral or from context, the noun **stays singular** — \"three book\", \"many book\"."
          ],
          "table": {
            "head": [
              "Sentence",
              "Noun form",
              "Meaning"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "*Гурван ном*",
                "singular",
                "three books"
              ],
              [
                "*Олон ном*",
                "singular",
                "many books"
              ],
              [
                "*Ном**ууд***",
                "plural",
                "the books (a particular group)"
              ],
              [
                "*Оюутн**ууд***",
                "plural",
                "the students"
              ],
              [
                "*Багш **нар***",
                "plural (people)",
                "the teachers"
              ]
            ]
          },
          "after": [
            "There are four suffixes — *-ууд, -үүд, -ууд, -нууд* following vowel harmony — plus a separate word, ***нар***, used only for **people**: *багш нар* (teachers), *эмч нар* (doctors), *та нар* (you all).",
            "**The practical rule: don't use a plural suffix until you're sure you really need one.** English speakers almost always make the mistake of adding too many, not too few. *Гурван номууд* is wrong; *гурван ном* is right."
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Things around you",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "tabel",
          "head": [
            "Монгол",
            "Say it",
            "English"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "*ном*",
              "*nom*",
              "book"
            ],
            [
